                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Let me tell you a story:\r\nI contacted the dev a long time ago (2019 i think) about a bunch of bugs. We started to chat, I sudmitted and showed a bunch of bugs which was more or less fixed. ALSO I made a google file with a bunch of ideas and he liked it, But in the end he just abandoned this game.\r\nThen he tells me about his idea for a new game and asks can I test earliest builds of it and give feedback.\r\nSo I tested a dozen of build for a new game (In the beginning there was nothing but a main view and an ability to build basic structures), and I told him a lot of ideas, which were implemented and the game evolved. I remember he had a macbook and was looking for investors on some Expo, he placed his macbook on some table they provided. This game right now called \"Anvil Saga\" and it's out. I didn't get any shoutouts or at least game key, not even a thank you even.",
